        "body": "Confirm that the expected account is active and assigned to the correct person. If sign-in fails, distinguish an incorrect credential from an account or connection issue before attempting recovery.Open the modules needed for the task. If a page or action is missing, have an authorized administrator check the assigned role and feature permissions.Check the relevant cameras separately. A visible module can still have a restricted camera scope, so confirm both the feature and resource permissions. Password recovery restores the ability to sign in; it does not expand a role or restore permissions that were never assigned. If recovery or access remains unresolved, provide the administrator with the account reference, affected module or camera, failure time, and error message. Keep passwords and active verification codes out of the investigation record. For implementation and handover, define access in terms of tasks: view a specified camera group, review historical footage, handle an event, or maintain configuration. Test each required task with the intended user role. An administrator’s successful test does not establish that an operator or investigator has the same access."
