        "heading": "Troubleshoot an Export",
        "body": "Check that the source footage exists and plays, the trim interval is valid, downloads are permitted, and the local disk has space. For larger exports, shorten the interval or split it into clips. Inspect task and download status before submitting another request. Formats, maximum duration, and file-size limits depend on the deployment. If a file does not open, verify that the download completed and try the project-recommended player. Retain the error, file size, and exported interval for investigation. Isolate the failure by stage: source playback, interval selection, export request, browser download, or local file playback. Retain the event or camera reference, selected interval, error message, and file size where a file was produced. Before repeating a request, check the current task and download state to avoid confusing an incomplete export with a second attempt."
